# =================================================================
# MASTER RECEPT & RULES FOR: KEEP TABS ON MEDIA (v.0.0001)
# =================================================================

[GLOBAL APP ARCHITECTURE]
- Language: Python 3.12+ using NiceGUI (FastAPI/Uvicorn running asynchronously).
- Layout: LOCKED in Landscape (horizontal) mode for kiosk-view on all touch devices.
- Visual Aesthetic: Dark mode, brushed metal design. UI buttons must be large and touch-friendly.

[DATABASE SAFETY & LOCK RULES (CHECKPOINT 1)]
- Main Database format: 'name_surname_city_date.sqlite3' (e.g., johan_andersson_stockholm_20260911.sqlite3).
- Startup Rule: Always start the application locked to the private owner database in read/write mode.
- External DB Rule: If opening a friend's database, enforce Read-Only mode on system level using SQLite URI: "file:path_to_db?mode=ro".
- UI Reaction: If active DB is Read-Only, automatically disable or hide all SCAN and SAVE buttons in NiceGUI using bindings.

[FAIR/EXPO MODES - "CHECK PRICE"]
- Create 'check_price_panel.py' inside 'ui/panels/' as a completely isolated tool.
- This panel MUST NOT have any connections or write-permissions to the SQLite database (no cursor.execute allowed).
- Flow: Scan barcode -> fetch live Discogs pricing via 'modules/services.py' -> compare asking price -> display color-coded Traffic Light (Green/Yellow/Red) + Warning if already owned in private DB.

[FUTURE RELEASE v.1.0 ROADMAP]
- Maintain clean, modular code to eventually support PyInstaller compilation.
- Ensure 'ui/panels/report_panel.py' can generate formatted Word/PDF documents via 'python-docx' for insurance companies to secure values for large collections up to 26,000 records.

